   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_ypQ8qSNhpMrDGsD9",
   "name": "Classifying Organic Reactions",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Classifying organic reactions"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The reactions of organic compounds can be classified into\n\n  - **Substitution**\n  - **Addition**\n  - **Combustion**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Substitution"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- A** substitution **reaction takes place when one functional group is replaced by another\n\n  - **Example: **Methane reacts with bromine under ultraviolet light"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**4**</sub>**    +    Br**<sub>**2**</sub>**       →            CH**<sub>**3**</sub>**Br   +    HBr**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**    methane + bromine   →   bromomethane + hydrogen bromide**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Addition"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- An **addition** reaction takes place when two or more molecules combine to form a larger molecule with no other products\n\n  - **Example: **Bromine will react with ethene and the bromine molecule will react and add across the double bond of the ethene"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**C**<sub>**2**</sub>**H**<sub>**4**</sub>**     +       Br**<sub>**2**</sub>**         →         C**<sub>**2**</sub>**H**<sub>**4**</sub>**Br**<sub>**2**</sub>"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**ethene   +   bromine   →   dibromoethane**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Combustion"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- This is the scientific term for burning. In a **combustion** reaction, an organic substance reacts with oxygen to form carbon dioxide (or carbon monoxide if incomplete combustion) and water.\n\n  - **Example: **Alkenes burn when heated in air of oxygen\n- If there is an unlimited supply of air / oxygen, the products are carbon dioxide and water\n- This is termed **complete** combustion"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**4**</sub>**   +   2O**<sub>**2**</sub>**   →   CO**<sub>**2**</sub>**   +   2H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**C**<sub>**3**</sub>**H**<sub>**8**</sub>**   +   5O**<sub>**2**</sub>**   →   3CO**<sub>**2**</sub>**   +   4H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O**"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- If there is a limited supply of air / oxygen, the products are carbon monoxide and water\n\n  - This is termed **incomplete** combustion"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**CH**<sub>**4**</sub>**   +   **$\\frac{3}{2}$**O**<sub>**2**</sub>**   →   CO   +   2H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O**"
  }
 ]
}